From ea7a842313f26522fc5cf64c2b96353f5468c423 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: anyingiit <49945850+anyingiit@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 21:58:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: add c.d.f. and w.r.t. to base abbreviation rules

Add c.d.f to REFERENCE_ABBRVS and w.r.t to INLINE_ONLY_ABBRVS so
text like "the c.d.f. F" and "w.r.t. V-TSMixer" is no longer split
into separate sentences.

Fixes #357
---
 CHANGELOG.md               | 1 +
 CONTRIBUTORS.md            | 1 +
 src/yasbd/rules/base.py    | 4 ++--
 tests/test_data/english.py | 3 +++
 4 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 2766be1..0cd0b22 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@ and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0
 ### Fixed
 
 - **Backtick-delimited quote sentence boundaries** ([#348](https://github.com/speedyk-005/yasbd-lib/pull/348)): Detect sentence boundaries after single/double backtick-delimited and doubled-apostrophe quoted text while preserving ordinary contractions.
+- **Base `c.d.f.` and `w.r.t.` abbreviations** ([#NNN](https://github.com/speedyk-005/yasbd-lib/pull/NNN)): Added `c.d.f` to base `REFERENCE_ABBRVS` and `w.r.t` to base `INLINE_ONLY_ABBRVS` so `the c.d.f. F` and `w.r.t. V-TSMixer` no longer split sentences.
 
 ...
 
